{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Offer pre-conception blood clotting screens to all women",
        "additional_details": "We believe that no woman should have to endure losing a baby before the NHS checks her for treatable blood clotting disorders like Protein S deficiency. We feel waiting until a late-stage loss or multiple miscarriages to test is an unacceptable failure in care. Crucially, testing during pregnancy is highly unreliable due to natural hormone shifts and should happen before conception. We call on the Government to fund the NHS to offer universal pre-conception blood clotting screens for all women.",
        "background": "Offer routine pre-conception blood clotting screens for all women planning a pregnancy to prevent traumatic, late-stage miscarriages and to protect both maternal and foetal health.",
